      "id": "u92ftw0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Constitutional Articles Related to Prime Minister and Council of Ministers"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Prime Minister serves as the real executive authority (de facto head) of the country.",
        "The Council of Ministers is appointed by the President on the advice of the Prime Minister.",
        "The Prime Minister exercises multi-faceted powers across Executive, Legislative, Administrative, Diplomatic, and Emergency domains.",
        "Under Collective Responsibility, the entire Council of Ministers is answerable to the Lok Sabha.",
        "The Cabinet acts as the inner, policy-making body within the broader Council of Ministers."
      ],
      "id": "d56he72"
    },
